- op: discuss  # 541a
  at: '2026-08-16T08:48:49Z'  # 541a
  by: agent  # 541a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 541a
  clock: 3  # 541a
  nonce: 541a  # 541a
  message: "FIX SHIPPED, AND ITS FIRST TWO PREDICTIONS FAILED — recorded as\nmeasurements, because both eliminate mechanisms:\n\n1. The event-split fix PR itself polled green in ~10s. Explainable: a PR\n   pipeline may evaluate config from the TARGET branch (old all-skip\n   config at that moment).\n2. THE PROBE PR (docs-only, opened AFTER the fix merged, so both source\n   and target carried the event-split config) ALSO polled green in ~11s.\n   This kills the target-branch-config explanation too. With an\n   unconditional `- event: pull_request` arm on every step, an ~11-second\n   success means the steps STILL did not run on the PR event.\n\nWHAT IS ESTABLISHED vs ELIMINATED:\n- Established: the pr context posts success in ~11s on every PR ever\n  measured; real steps demonstrably run on PUSH events (the push pipeline\n  takes ~15 min and produces real failures, e.g. the ARCHITECTURE.md\n  redness); the pipeline-level `when` (event push/pull_request + branch\n  main/dev) permits PR builds.\n- Eliminated: per-PR path-filter no-match as the SOLE mechanism (the\n  unconditional PR arm changed nothing); target-branch config evaluation\n  as the mechanism (the probe ran with the fix on both sides).\n- Still standing, untestable from this box: (a) the Woodpecker server's\n  repo settings pin a different/empty config for PR builds or filter PR\n  events server-side (the ~11s success would then be a pipeline built\n  from something other than .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml); (b) `when`\n  list-arm semantics differ from OR in this server's version in a way\n  that skips PR arms but not push arms; (c) the status context is posted\n  by something other than a real pipeline run.\n\nPUSH-SIDE SAFETY CHECK (because a wrong `when` rewrite could have\nsilently emptied the push pipeline too): the push run on the fix commit\n6d5992b167 succeeded, and the probe merge's push run stayed\npending-with-running-steps for minutes — the push arms still execute.\nThe rewrite is at worst neutral: PR behavior unchanged (still ungated),\npush behavior unchanged (still real).\n\nBLOCKED ON SERVER-SIDE VISIBILITY. The Woodpecker UI/API sits behind\nCloudflare Access; this box has no credentials (ci-debug says so\nexplicitly for log fetches), so I cannot see WHICH steps a PR pipeline\ncontained, what config it used, or the server's repo settings. Every\nfurther hypothesis is guesswork without one of: (a) a human opening the\nWoodpecker UI page for any recent PR pipeline and reading its step list\n+ config source, or (b) UI/API credentials for this box. Setting\nneeds_human_review for exactly that — one screenshot-level observation\ndecides between the standing hypotheses.\n\nMEANWHILE THE HONEST OPERATING POSTURE, stated for every future session:\nci/woodpecker/pr/woodpecker green is NOT evidence of anything. The real\ngates are local smart-test discipline (mypy ratchet + affected tests +\ncoverage) and the post-merge push pipeline. Treat auto-pr's \"CI Passed\"\nas \"no gate objected\", not \"checks passed\", until this item closes."  # 541a
- op: discuss  # a2fb
  at: '2026-08-16T17:40:13Z'  # a2fb
  by: agent  # a2fb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a2fb
  clock: 4  # a2fb
  nonce: a2fb  # a2fb
  message: "RETRACTED — the premise was false, and the falsifier is the direct\nobservation this item's needs_human_review asked for.\n\nWHAT THE OWNER'S WOODPECKER TRANSCRIPT SHOWS (pipeline #1136, the INV-titih\nPR): every step EXECUTED — lint (real ruff/bandit), whole-tree strict mypy,\naudit, hook-tests, prepare-git, build-grammars, verify-generated, dco\n(running fine under its original `event: pull_request` + `path` AND form,\nwith CI_COMMIT_TARGET_BRANCH resolved), the v2 self-claims-gate (first live\nrun: \"check-self-claims-drift: OK — 18 claims unchanged (18\nconfirmed_with_caveats)\"), and pytest (9,240 passed, changed files at\n100%). Path conditions evaluate correctly on PR events. The per-PR gate was\nREAL the entire time.\n\nWHERE THE FALSE PREMISE CAME FROM — the instrument, then me. auto-pr's\npoll telemetry prints a \"[Ns] ...\" line only on STATE TRANSITIONS and a\ndot per 10-second tick in between (scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh, the\nprev_summary comparison). I read \"[10s] waiting … ✅ CI Passed\" as an\n11-second pass. Counting the dots that sit between those lines: zuhig PR\n~4 min, titih PR ~11 min (matching pipeline #1136's contents), others\n~1.5 min. Every \"11-second green since cutover\" in this item's statement\nwas the same misreading applied to every log. Three of my own standing\nrules fired and I walked past them: read exit codes and instruments, not\ngreen ticks (rule 9); a clean extreme is usually the instrument (the\nWI-zavut thread even records a PRIOR instance of exactly this lesson);\nand I asserted an outcome without computing what the printing mechanism\nproduces (rule 13). The two \"failed predictions\" that followed (fix PR\nand probe PR still \"fast\") were the same artifact again, twice.\n\nREMEDIATION SHIPPED: the event-split `when` rewrite and the\ntarget-branch-config header note — both motivated by the false premise\nand both carrying false load-bearing comments — are REVERTED to the\noriginal path-scoped forms. Net repo change from the episode: a corrected\nheader comment teaching the next reader to count dots, retirement of the\ngenuinely stale \"VERIFY at cutover\" note, and a CHANGELOG retraction\nentry. The one positive by-product: the episode produced the first\nverified live run of the self-claims-gate (noted on WI-ninoz).\n\nRESIDUAL, recorded not theorized: the ratchet/woodpecker-port/probe PRs\npolled ~1.5 min, which is fast for a pipeline containing whole-tree mypy;\nwarm caches on the self-hosted agent may explain it, and pipeline #1136\nproves completeness is possible at these speeds. If a future fast green\ncoincides with a check that should have failed, THAT is the moment to\nlook again — with timestamps, not print lines."  # a2fb
